DECISIONS 215 (the checker sees the lexer's findings, as in a build): a literal holding a lexer error (E1109 here) has the error type, so it draws no second finding from the check of its annotation, a default or an operand. Each error below is the lexer's alone.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local let s: String = "x\q"

local let n: Int = "x\q"

local record R {
  d: String = "\z"
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E1109]  a/a.canon:3:25
  invalid escape sequence "\q"

error[E1109]  a/a.canon:5:22
  invalid escape sequence "\q"

error[E1109]  a/a.canon:8:16
  invalid escape sequence "\z"

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
